<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar outflows at $5.9 mln May 23.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar outflows at $5.9 mln May 23.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $5.9 million deficit on May 23 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data suplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the Central Bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON MAY 23</p>
<p>Exports: $213.4 million</p>
<p>Imports: $267.6 million</p>
<p>Finanancial buy: $343.5 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $295.2 million</p>
<p>Net deficit: $5.9 million</p>
<p>MAY DOLLAR FLOWS UP DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $4.096 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $4.240 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $5.294 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $4.059 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $1.091 billion</p>
<p>Note: Figures rounded off.</p>
<p>((--Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroon, 55 11 2485418))</p>
</text>
